    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's exactly my point. the fact that we're \"wired\" to seek meaning in a vacuum just proves how broken it is. we're basically programmed to chase ghosts. if the only reason to keep going is just a biological drive to avoid death, doesn't that make the drive itself pretty hollow? it's like being trapped in a movie that has no plot, but you're forced to stay in the theater forever because your instincts won't let you leave. doesn't it seem more logical to just stop playing when there's no actual prize at the end?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
